# Agile Workflow (Lightweight)

Source of truth for tickets: `docs/backlog.md`. No sprint ceremonies, velocity, or story points.

## Hierarchy

- **Epic (`E-###`)**: Multi-story outcome. Never an implementation unit.
- **Story (`S-###`)**: One user-visible value. As a / I want / so that + Given/When/Then. **Always the unit of delivery.**
- **Task (`T-###`)**: One behavior that advances the story. One TDD cycle, one commit. No horizontal splits (schema-only, UI-only, repository-only).

## Before coding

1. Confirm the target Story ID in `docs/backlog.md`. If missing, add the story first.
2. Work on **one in-progress story** per session / PR.
3. Split the story if any of these hold: more than 5 acceptance criteria; roughly more than 8 files touched; cannot finish in one session; phrased as "whole feature" or "build all infrastructure first".

## Vertical slices only

- Slice by **user value**, not by technical layer.
- Good: "Save one stamp from the camera"
- Bad: "Create table", "Add repository", "Build screen shell"

Within one slice, prefer a unified implementation (do not fragment files without need).

## Definition of Done (story)

- Acceptance criteria are covered by tests
- Each task completed Red → Green per `tdd-cycle` rule
- `pnpm run check` passed after each task
- One commit per task (message includes Story ID, e.g. `S-001`)
- `docs/backlog.md` task checkboxes updated
- Do not start the next story until the current story is Done

## Exceptions (no story required)

- `chore`: dependencies, tooling, config
- Time-boxed spikes: leave no production code
